      en: ["Established in 1957, Bako is the oldest national park in Sarawak.", "It covers a small area of 27 square kilometers on the Muara Tebas peninsula.", "The park is renowned for its population of around 275 proboscis monkeys.", "Bako contains seven distinct types of vegetation and ecosystems.", "The park is only accessible via a 20-minute boat ride from the village of Kampung Bako.", "There are 16 marked walking trails for visitors to explore.", "The famous sea stack, a geological formation, is one of the park's most photographed landmarks.", "The Bornean bearded pig is a common sight, often scavenging for food around the park headquarters."],
